    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d180">

                <pb facs="0203" n="129" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg129"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/6723</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum Dictated in the Office of the Assistant
                        Secretary of State by the British Ambassador</hi><anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d180-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>The Hague</placeName>, <date
                        ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1917-07-16">July 16, 1917</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>Austrian Legation stated that in the course of the negotiations between the
                    Emperor of Austria and Kaiser Wilhelm,
                        Hindenburg had declared that under
                    no circumstances could Germany adopt a program of a peace without annexation.
                    Disruption and national bankruptcy would be the necessary consequence of a peace
                    in which Germany recognized the commercial independence of Belgium.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d180-f1" n="3" type="source" xml:id="d180-f1-content">
                <p>Paraphrase of a telegram from The Hague, dated July 16, 1917.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
